title: The M-Apparat
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and c_m_apparat_timer <= 0 and year >= 1921
on-arrival: c_m_apparat_timer = 5; month_actions += 1
frequency: 150
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs

= The M-Apparat

The party has a secret department now: the military-political apparatus, known to the few who know of it as the M-Apparat. It collects intelligence on the Reichswehr and the right, trains instructors for the workers' militias, and keeps lists of weapons. [? if comintern_member = 1 : Officers sent by the Red Army's staff advise it, and Moscow pays for much of it. ?]

[? if march_action = 1 : After March, everyone agrees the party was not ready to fight. They do not agree on what to do about it. ?] [? if c_m_apparat_built >= 2 : The apparatus has grown large enough that the police have started looking for it. ?]

- @build: Expand the apparatus.
- @inward: Turn it to protecting the party.
- @small: Keep it small, and under the Zentrale's control.
- @easy_discard

@build
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. More arms and trained men; more police attention. The Left approves.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.c_m_apparat_built += 1;
Q.red_guards_arms += 6;
Q.red_guards_strength += 1;
Q.repression += 3 + Q.c_m_apparat_built;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 6;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 3;
if (Q.comintern_member) {
    Q.independence -= 3;
}
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

Instructors are trained in a forest lodge in Thuringia, and arms are bought from Reichswehr quartermasters who need the money. Every new cell is another secret that can be betrayed.

@inward
subtitle: Watch the Freikorps, spot the informers. The party is harder to strike.
on-arrival: {!
Q.repression -= 4;
Q.red_guards_loyalty += 5;
Q.unity += 2;
Q['lean_' + Q.leading_faction] += 1;
!}

The apparatus turns its attention to the police spies inside our own districts. Two are found in Berlin, one in Halle. The right-wing leagues' meeting places are watched.

@small
subtitle: The Spartacists are relieved; the Left calls it cowardice.
on-arrival: {!
Q.unity += 3;
Q.independence += 2;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 4;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 4;
Q.militancy -= 2;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

The Zentrale decides that a party of workers does not need a general staff. The apparatus is reduced to a few couriers and a filing cabinet.
